SectionTrain draws a pretreatment train as one sectional elevation on a limestone sheet, every vessel cut open so its bed shows and each bed holding what it caught, so the reader sees the water lose its particles, hardness, chlorine and fines stage by stage.

- On the site: a `diagram` block with `"look": "section-train"` (renderer `assets/src/blocks/look-section-train.js`), on sys-pretreatment "How the train is built". No concept image of its own: adapted from compliance.3 (cutaway) and systems.0 (one continuous run, a label column per stage); the cross-section with contaminants dropping out is this page's own idea.
- Markup: `<div class="aq-section-train" data-theme="light">` (light tokens on the fixed limestone ground) → `svg.__defs` (hatch pattern, lens clips), `svg.__svg` (one 200-unit column per stage: `__pipe`/`__bore` twin wall, `__flow` water, `g.__col` per stage with the cut vessel: `__wall` hatched, `__in` interior, `__bed` marks, `__seep` the water's way through the bed, `g.__caught` glyphs; `__lens` at feed and outlet; the monitoring `__bus` with `__bubble` instruments; `__swarm` and `__drop` for motion only), `ol.__stages` (a column per stage: `__mini` the same column cut out for phones, `__no`, `h3.__t` (a link when the stage has one), `__d`, `__catch` chip with its glyph), `p.__base` (the block's base line on a dashed mark).
- Fields: `h`, `stages [{t, d, link, cut, catch}]`, `base`. New optional per stage: `cut` ("feed", "tank", "media", "softener", "carbon", "cartridge", "out"; default: first feed, last out, else media) picks the column's drawing; `catch` `{g, t}`: the glyph its bed holds (`p` particles, `h` hardness, `c` chlorine, `f` fines) and its short name for the chip.
- Glyphs: particles solid dots, hardness hexagon crystals, chlorine crosses, fines dust. The feed lens shows all but fines (fines come from the beds); the outlet lens shows clean water only.
- Drawn inline, not with IsoKit (a flat section, not an isometric view): vessels, beds, lenses, the backflow preventer, the bus. Same stroke family: 1.5 px `on-limestone` walls, 1 px detail, `flow` water.
- Phones: the elevation is cut into one frame per stage (`__mini`), run down the page on a pipe rail at the left with the text beside each.
- Use it for a train of four to eight stages where what each stage removes is the point. Where only the order matters use WindingRoute or ProcessDiagram.

## Motion

Motion: one timeline when the drawing is 30 % into view. The vessels rise into place like a print, the pipe draws and the feed lens opens; then the water runs the route once with a cluster of contaminant glyphs riding it. As the water reaches each bed, the kind it catches leaves the cluster and settles into the bed, the stage number turns `flow` and its chip strikes; fines settle on the cartridge; the outlet lens opens clean. About 4 s. Phones: each frame rises and its caught glyphs settle as it scrolls in. Nothing under reduced motion.
